@@section 3
@@title SQ-CMP Corpse decay on world time, 2026-11-18 ([plan_corpses.md](../plan_corpses.md) 3.1, TODO `corpses #1`, `corpses #6`)
@@date 2026-11-18
@@jars creativecompat
@@sources feature_writeup/plan_corpses.md
@@text
@@text Corpses are summoned with a `Death` compound (Corpse mod NBT) and Compat's `creativecompat:corpse` state; a `DeathTime` in the past stands in for days of play. Times are the defaults in `[corpses]` (creativecompat-common.toml).
@@text
@@table
## SQ-CMP-10 | Corpse mixins apply; the config section exists
@group A
@commands Any boot with Corpse and the current Compat jar; read `config/creativecompat-common.toml`
@pass `CorpseDecayMixin` applies (no mixin error); the file has `[corpses]` with `skeletonTime = 168000`, `emptySkeletonTime = 600`, `emptyDespawnTime = 6000`, the four Nether times and both dimension lists
@fails a target name in `CorpseDecayMixin` (m_8119_, m_7380_, m_7378_, m_8097_, m_5446_) no longer matches the Corpse jar
@reviewed 2026-11-25
bootreject CorpseDecayMixin.*(Error|error|failed)
shell grep -nE "^\s*\[corpses\]|skeletonTime|emptyDespawnTime|netherWitherTime|noDecayDimensions" config/creativecompat-common.toml
look the [corpses] section with the default values
@reviewed 2026-11-22

## SQ-CMP-11 | A full corpse turns skeleton 7 days after death, caught up on load
@group A
@commands Shortened `[corpses] skeletonTime = 200` and a restart (stands in for 7 days); `forceload add 0 0`; advance the clock 300 ticks; `summon corpse:corpse 2 -60 2 {Tags:["c11a"],Death:{PlayerName:"Test",MainInventory:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:stone",Count:1b}]},"creativecompat:corpse":{DeathTime:1L}}` and a second with `Tags:["c11b"]` and no `creativecompat:corpse`; wait 3 s; read each `Stage`
@pass c11a: `Stage: 1b` (skeleton; its death was more than skeletonTime ticks of game time ago); c11b: `Stage: 0b` with a `DeathTime` near the current game time
@fails c11a stays 0: the decay check does not run (tick redirect or config gate); c11b turns skeleton at once: DeathTime defaulted to 0
@reviewed 2026-11-25
@absent creativecompat:corpse (an NBT compound key on the corpse entity, not a registry id)
# r1120fix (2026-11-20): a negative DeathTime is the mixin's "unset" sentinel (CorpseDecayMixin: deathTime < 0 -> now - age),
# so the r1120nv fixture read as just died. Now: skeletonTime 200 ticks (restart), the clock moved past 300 ticks, and a
# positive DeathTime 1 (game tick 1); the default is put back at the end of the row
edit python3 "$INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py" toml config/creativecompat-common.toml corpses skeletonTime 200
restart
> forceload add 0 0
sleep 3
> cdevtest tickwarp 300
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done ticks=300 120
> time query gametime
capture GT The time is (\d+)
> summon corpse:corpse 2 -60 2 {Tags:["c11a"],Death:{PlayerName:"Test",MainInventory:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:stone",Count:1b}]},"creativecompat:corpse":{DeathTime:1L}}
> summon corpse:corpse 4 -60 2 {Tags:["c11b"],Death:{PlayerName:"Test",MainInventory:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:stone",Count:1b}]}}
sleep 3
> data get entity @e[tag=c11a,limit=1] "creativecompat:corpse".Stage
expect has the following entity data: 1b
> data get entity @e[tag=c11b,limit=1] "creativecompat:corpse".Stage
expect has the following entity data: 0b
> data get entity @e[tag=c11b,limit=1] "creativecompat:corpse".DeathTime
look c11b DeathTime is near the game time {GT} (within a few hundred ticks), not 0
> kill @e[tag=c11a]
> kill @e[tag=c11b]
shell python3 "$INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py" toml config/creativecompat-common.toml corpses skeletonTime 168000
reject (Unknown or incomplete command|Incorrect argument for command|No entity was found|\[cdevtest\] verb=tickwarp .*done=0)

