## CQ-CMP-14 | Corpse look: armor follows contents, wither skeleton in the Nether
@group client
@commands Survival client: die in the overworld wearing iron armor and holding a sword; open the corpse, take the helmet and the sword; close. Then summon the c13b corpse of SQ-CMP-13 in the Nether next to you with `ArmorInventory:[{Slot:3b,id:"minecraft:golden_helmet",Count:1b}]` in its `Death`
@pass LOOK: within a second the corpse no longer wears the helmet or holds the sword, the rest of the armor stays; the Nether corpse is a normal-size skeleton with the dark wither skeleton texture, wearing the gold helmet
@fails armor still shown: `followContents` off or the renderer still caches its dummy; wither corpse big: drawn with the wither skeleton renderer instead of the skeleton model
@absent creativecompat:corpse (an NBT compound key on the corpse entity, not a registry id)
# drafted r1124gate (2026-11-24): single-player client (`qrun.py client`) or `qrun.py pair`; every command names
# PerfEval (the capture client's player), none uses @s, so `>` runs as the player or on the server console alike.
# Corpse menu indices (Corpse 1.0.17 + Compat): 0-3 armor helmet first, 4 offhand, 5-31 main, 32-40 hotbar,
# 41-76 player inventory, 77-80 cosmetic helmet to boots, 81+ curios sorted by slot id (back, belt, necklace, ring).
> gamerule keepInventory false
> gamerule doImmediateRespawn true
> fill -4 100 -4 6 100 8 minecraft:stone
> fill -4 101 -4 6 104 8 minecraft:air
> kill @e[type=corpse:corpse]
sleep 1
> kill @e[type=item]
> clear PerfEval
> curios clear PerfEval
> spawnpoint PerfEval 0 101 0
> gamemode survival PerfEval
