## SQ-CMP-17 | Corpse sections: mixins apply, config keys, a corpse holding only section items is not empty
@group A
@commands Any boot with Corpse, Curios and the current Compat jar; read `config/creativecompat-common.toml`; `forceload add 0 0`; summon a corpse whose only items are one curio-tagged and one cosmetic-tagged stack in its additional items (`Items`); wait 40 s (past the 30 s empty skeleton time); read its `Stage` and `EmptiedAt`
@pass the five common section mixins apply (no mixin error); `[corpses]` has `sectionedScreen = true`, `curioCap = 24`; c17: `Stage: 0b`, `EmptiedAt: -1L` (it holds items, so neither the empty skeleton nor the 5 min rule runs)
@fails Stage 1b: section stacks were left out of the empty check (only the Additional Items checks may skip them); a mixin error naming `lambda$openCorpseGUI$1`, `m_38946_`, `transferItems`, `m_7648_` or `executeServerSide`: the Corpse jar changed
@absent creativecompat:corpse creativecompat:curio (NBT keys on the corpse and on stacks, not registry ids)
