## CQ-CMP-19 | Corpse sections: take, shift-click and Transfer Items put each item back where it was
@group client
@commands Survival client, same kit as CQ-CMP-18 plus a stack of extra items that go to Additional Items (a modded drop, for example a backpack's spill); die; (a) open the corpse, shift-click one curio, drag another into the inventory, press a hotbar number over a cosmetic piece; (b) die again with the full kit, put a different ring in the first ring slot, then open the corpse and press Transfer Items
@pass (a) each taken item stacks with a fresh copy of the same item (no hidden tags; F3+H shows no `creativecompat:curio` or `Cosmetic*` keys); the section slot empties; Additional Items holds only the extra items; (b) every curio returns to the exact slot type and index it was in at death, the ring whose slot is taken goes to another ring slot or the inventory; cosmetic pieces go back to their cosmetic slots; nothing keeps a section tag
@fails a curio in the wrong index of its type: the transfer packet hook ran after Corpse Curios Compat; a taken item does not stack: the tag strip missed a path (shift-click is `m_7648_`, hotbar swap is `onTake`); section items also on the Additional Items pages: the filtered view did not replace the container's inventory; run alone in a fresh client the corpse opens Additional Items or logs `IndexOutOfBoundsException: Index 90` on content packets: the main-screen redirect in `CorpseGuisMixin` or the `setSlots` trim in `CorpseAdditionalContainerMixin` is missing (creative-compat-publish #20)
