@commands Survival client, same kit as CQ-CMP-18 plus an elytra in the Elytra Slot back slot and one curio with its render toggled off (the eye button on its Curios slot); die; look at the corpse from the front and the back, take a screenshot (F2); then take the elytra and one visible curio out of the corpse and look again after a second; done together with the CQ-CMP-18 screenshot look-check
@pass LOOK (screenshot to the owner with CQ-CMP-18): the corpse's player model shows the curios that draw on the player (belt, necklace, back items) and the elytra on its back over the chestplate, as the player looked before death; the render-toggled curio does not show; after the items are taken (within a second) they no longer show; the living player's own curios are unaffected
@fails no curios on the model: the dummy player's curios handler was not filled (no `Curios` list in the synced section tag, or the `RenderPlayerEvent.Pre` listener did not reach `CorpseCuriosClient.fill`); the elytra missing while curios show: Elytra Slot's layer reads another source; the toggled curio shows: the `Hidden` flag was not recorded at death; taken items still show: the fill is not redone on a resync
@sources feature_writeup/plan_corpses.md
@reviewed 2026-11-22
