## SQ-CMP-23 | [mixins] keys written, every gated mod in its tested range, exact Breezy gate
@group A
@commands Boot 1; read `config/creativecompat-common.toml`; grep the log for range warnings and the Breezy mixin
@pass `[mixins]` table with 36 keys (one per `MixinSwitches` entry; 32 before the wave 2 melting switches, 2026-11-24), all `true`; no `is outside the tested range` and no `is not [` line from `[creativecompat]`; the `SupplementariesBreezyCompatMixin` gate passes (pack has Supplementaries 1.19.2-2.4.20, Breezy 1.0.8: no `is not [` line; the mixin itself applies only on a client, when a wind vane first ticks); `python3 $INST/tools/scratch_query/cmp_mixin_check.py` shows no mixin skipped that applied in r1122cc
@fails a range string wrong for the installed version (the mod's mixins go missing); the config spec missing `[mixins]`
@boot 1
@reviewed 2026-11-25
bootexpect \[creativecompat\] loaded \(config/
bootreject \[creativecompat\].*(outside the tested range|is not \[)
# 2026-11-24 (r1124gate BATCH-FAULT): 36 keys since the four wave 2 melting switches (MeltingBlockState, BiomeMelt, VanillaLightMelt, EndFire)
shell n=$(awk '/^\[mixins\]/{m=1;next} /^\[/{m=0} m && /=/' config/creativecompat-common.toml | grep -c "= true"); echo "true keys $n"; test "$n" = 36
shell grep -c "SupplementariesBreezyCompatMixin" logs/debug.log; python3 $INST/tools/scratch_query/cmp_mixin_check.py | tail -5
# r1123cx (2026-11-23): BreezyCompatImpl is called only by a ticking wind vane on a client, so on a dedicated server the mixin never applies; the row checks the gate
look 36 true keys; no Breezy gate warning; cmp_mixin_check skips only absent-mod mixins and the client-only Breezy one

## SQ-CMP-38 | With Snow! Real Magic loaded its fall handles snow; salt layers keep the pack's fall
@group A
@commands Boot 1 (full pack, Snow! Real Magic 6.5.4 in it); two stone pillars at y 115 to 116 with a snow 3 and a salt 3 on top; remove the upper stones; read the landed blocks and the log
@pass log line `Snow! Real Magic loaded: snow falls by its snowGravity` once; the snow lands as `minecraft:snow` at y 116; the salt lands as `vintagedelight:salt[layers=3]` at y 116 (never snow); no `creativecompat:falling_layer` entity for the snow
@fails no log line or a pack falling entity for snow: `FallingLayers.falls` not gating snow (`srmLoaded`); salt landed as snow: Snow! Real Magic's own tick fell it (its `tick` on every `SnowLayerBlock`, B3; step 11 of snow_real_magic.md); salt gone or floating: the pack hold missed; snow floating: Snow! Real Magic `snowGravity` off in its config
@boot 1
@reviewed 2026-11-24
@absent creativecompat:falling_layer (Compat entity type, missing from the last /dumpall registry dump)
bootexpect \[creativecompat\] Snow! Real Magic loaded: snow falls by its snowGravity
> forceload add 0 0
> setblock 0 115 0 minecraft:stone
> setblock 0 116 0 minecraft:stone
> setblock 0 117 0 minecraft:snow[layers=3]
> setblock 3 115 0 minecraft:stone
> setblock 3 116 0 minecraft:stone
> setblock 3 117 0 vintagedelight:salt[layers=3]
sleep 1
> setblock 0 116 0 minecraft:air
> setblock 3 116 0 minecraft:air
> execute if entity @e[type=creativecompat:falling_layer,x=0,y=116,z=0,distance=..3] run say CMP38_SNOW_PACK_ENTITY
sleep 5
> execute if block 0 116 0 minecraft:snow run say CMP38_SNOW_LANDED
> execute if block 3 116 0 vintagedelight:salt[layers=3] run say CMP38_SALT_LANDED
waitlog CMP38_SALT_LANDED 20
expect CMP38_SNOW_LANDED
reject CMP38_SNOW_PACK_ENTITY
shell grep -c "Snow! Real Magic loaded: snow falls by its snowGravity" logs/latest.log; true
look the hand-over line once (logged at mod construction); both layers landed at y 116
> fill 0 115 0 3 117 0 minecraft:air

