## SQ-CMP-27 | The four old [jei] page switches carry over into [jei] pagesOff
@group A
@commands Boot 1 (prep writes `seasoningCategory = false`, `canCategories = true`, `potionBucketCategory = true`, `tippedArrowCategory = false`); read `config/creativecompat-common.toml`; restart and read again
@pass log `[jei] page switches carried over to pagesOff = [seasoning, tipped_arrows]` once; the file has `pagesOff = ["seasoning", "tipped_arrows"]` and none of the four old keys; after the restart no second carry-over line and the list is unchanged
@fails no carry-over line: `JeiPageKeys.carryOver` not called before `registerConfig` in `CreativeCompat`, or the file has no `[jei]` table; old keys still there: Forge read the file before the carry-over
@reviewed 2026-11-25
@boot 1
# 2026-11-24 (r1124gate BATCH-FAULT): a bootexpect reads the boot after the restart; the first boot's line is checked in its kept log
shell grep -nE "pagesOff|seasoningCategory|canCategories|potionBucketCategory|tippedArrowCategory" config/creativecompat-common.toml
restart
shell n=$(cat logs/qrun_boot*.log | grep -c "\[jei\] page switches carried over to pagesOff = \[seasoning, tipped_arrows\]"); echo "first boot carry-over lines $n"; test "$n" = 1
shell grep -c "page switches carried over" logs/latest.log; grep -n "pagesOff" config/creativecompat-common.toml
look first boot: one carry-over line, `pagesOff = ["seasoning", "tipped_arrows"]`, no old key; after the restart 0 carry-over lines and the same list

## SQ-CMP-28 | Hops vine keeps its own shears handling; other modded vines still get fertile
@group A
@commands Same boot: `/setblock 0 120 0 botania:solid_vine[fertile=false]`, `/setblock 2 120 0 hearthandharvest:hops_vine[fertile=false]`, then `/setblock 2 120 0 hearthandharvest:hops_vine`
@pass the Botania vine is placed with `fertile=false`; the hops vine command fails with an unknown-property error naming `fertile` and the plain hops vine places (Creative Delight registers the hops vine with `VineShearing.keepOwnHandling`)
@fails the hops vine has `fertile`: Creative Delight's `CompatRegistrations.register` ran after the blocks were built, or the class name changed; Botania without it: `VineBlockShearMixin` not applied
@boot 1
@reviewed 2026-11-25
> setblock 0 120 0 botania:solid_vine[fertile=false]
> setblock 2 120 0 hearthandharvest:hops_vine[fertile=false]
> setblock 2 120 0 hearthandharvest:hops_vine
sleep 2
> execute if block 0 120 0 botania:solid_vine[fertile=false] run say SOLID_VINE_FERTILE_STATE
> execute if block 2 120 0 hearthandharvest:hops_vine run say HOPS_PLACED
waitlog HOPS_PLACED 20
shell grep -E "SOLID_VINE_FERTILE_STATE|HOPS_PLACED|fertile" logs/latest.log | tail -5
look SOLID_VINE_FERTILE_STATE and HOPS_PLACED said; the hops vine line with fertile is an unknown-property error

## SQ-CMP-29 | Treated-stick tomatoes stay in the idle random tick rules from Creative Delight
@group A
@commands Same boot: grep the log for idle random tick rule warnings; place a grown treated-stick tomato and a rope above it with the server running
@pass no `[perf] idleRandomTickRules: skipped` line for `creativedelight:treated_stick_tomatoes`; the grown vine still climbs a stick placed above it (wake_above) as before
@fails the rule is missing: `IdleTickRules.addModRule` not called from Creative Delight's constructor, or `IdleRandomTicks` built before it
@boot 1
@draft the climb check needs the treated-stick block id and its grown state written in; a runner fills them from the CD block list

## CQ-CMP-30 | JEI grouped pages follow [jei] pagesOff
@group client
@commands Client on the SQ-CMP-27 config (`pagesOff = ["seasoning", "tipped_arrows"]`); open JEI on salt, an empty can, a potion bucket and a tipped arrow; then set `pagesOff = []` and `/reload`
@pass with the list: no Seasoning or Tipped Arrows page (their recipes on Crafting / Mixing / Spout pages), Canning, Using Cans and Potion Buckets pages shown; with the empty list all six pages shown
@fails a page shown while listed: its plugin still reads an old key, or the id is spelled differently from `CompatConfig.Jei.pageOn` callers (`FlavorJEI`, `CanPagesJEI`, `PotionPagesJEI`)
@reviewed 2026-11-24
